    {
      "id": "surrealist",
      "name": "The Surrealist Dreamer",
      "description": "The line between waking and dreaming is where you feel most at home. You are drawn to art that operates beneath the surface — symbolic, allegorical, psychologically charged. Works that make you look twice, that hide meanings within meanings, that blur reality just enough to reveal something deeper. Logic is overrated. You do not collect art for its face value; you collect it for everything it does not say out loud.",
      "image": "https:\/\/images.metmuseum.org\/CRDImages\/ep\/original\/DP-14201-023.jpg",
      "recommendations": [
